:root { --bg: #faf8f4; --text: #2a2520; --accent: #8b6914; --accent-dark: #6b4f0e; --subtle: #d4c9b0; --verse-bg: #f0e8d4; --verse-border: #c9a84c; --source-color: #7a6530; --aramaic-color: #5a4a2a; --os-color: #5a3e1b; --summary-bg: #eef3e8; --summary-border: #6b8f4a; }

* { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }

body { font-family: 'EB Garamond', 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif; background-color: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.85; font-size: 18px; max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 30px 80px; }

.main-header { text-align: center; padding: 30px 0 40px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--subtle); margin-bottom: 40px; }

.main-header .series-title { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif; font-size: 14px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 4px; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 8px; }

.main-header h1 { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif; font-size: 36px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-dark); margin-bottom: 6px; }

.main-header .subtitle { font-size: 16px; color: var(--source-color); font-style: italic; }

p { text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 18px; hyphens: auto; }

.section-header { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--os-color); margin: 38px 0 18px; padding-bottom: 6px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--subtle); }

.aramaic { font-style: italic; color: var(--aramaic-color); }

.key-term { font-style: italic; color: var(--accent-dark); }

.source { font-size: 15px; color: var(--source-color); }

.scripture { font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent-dark); }

.translator-summary { background: var(--summary-bg); border: 2px solid var(--summary-border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 28px 26px; margin: 50px 0 30px; }

.translator-summary h3 { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif; font-size: 20px; color: var(--summary-border); margin-bottom: 14px; text-align: center; letter-spacing: 1px; }

.translator-summary p { font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 12px; }

.translator-summary .translator-note { font-size: 14px; color: #666; text-align: center; margin-top: 16px; font-style: italic; }

Likutay Halachos · Choshen Mishpat

Hilchos G'viyas Chov Min HaLikuchos V'Apotiki 5 — Part 1

Laws of Collecting a Debt from Purchasers and the Apotiki — 5 (§§1–7) · Based on "Teekoo" — Likutay Moharan II:1 · The great Lender, t'filah, the lien upon land, and the three avodos

Based on the Torah "Teekoo" 1 in Likutay Tinyana, Siman 1. See there the entire Torah.

And this is the aspect of the fact that the essential lien of the debt takes effect upon land specifically. For all the loans are drawn from the blemish of the aspects discussed in the aforementioned Torah. For it is explained there that the true Tzadik who constantly engages in t'filah [prayer] in ultimate perfection — he is the aspect of the great Lender, from whom everything receives and borrows. As is found in the Zohar: "All the stars borrow one from another; the moon borrows from the sun" etc. See there.
